name w1-04-bvr-pair-1
timeout 600

# CAMPAIGN W1, SORTIE 4 OF 10 - THE BVR INTERCEPT, TWO AGAINST TWO, RUNG 4 OF THE LADDER.
# Spec, anchor and sources: doc/campaigns/w1-red-flag.md. Format: doc/missions/campaign.md.
# CONTROL: w1-03-bvr-single.fbm. Same lane, same entry longitudes, same altitude, same racks; the ONE
# degree of freedom this rung adds is the SECOND AIRCRAFT A SIDE and the two flights that come with it.
# It is the THIRD geometry the saturation gate's doctrine sweep is flown on (doc/doctrine-evolution.md
# section 4.2, S2).
#
# THE ARENA is w1-01's lane at full length (93.9 km, `--elev const`, 0 m range floor); the anchor and the
# substitution's direction are in w1-01-merge.fbm.
#
# THE ONE TACTICAL QUESTION: does the cooperative sort hold TWO DISTINCT targets through the whole run,
# and what does the cover rule cost when both members reach Rtr at once?
#
# THE ASYMMETRY IS NOT MISSION DATA - it is what the two modules ARE (doc/formation.md section 7,
# doc/modules/mig29/datalink-gci.md 5.1):
#   channel  F-16: MIDS-LVT, every member transmitting its own fix, its flight position and a target
#            POINT with a "my round still needs me" bit, once a second. MiG-29: NOTHING - the 9-12 has no
#            cooperative terminal at all, so its sort is the BRIEFED contract (`set brief_sort left`)
#            applied by each pilot to the picture he personally has.
#   cover    the rule that keeps one member free is the same on both sides and its PRICE is not: an
#            AIM-120 binds its shooter 0.3 s, an R-27R 17.3 s - a factor of 58 [MESS,
#            doc/formation.md] - and the MiG has no channel on which "my leader is bound" could travel,
#            so its deferral is 0 s BY CONSTRUCTION rather than by choice. THE COVER QUESTION IS
#            THEREFORE CHEAP FOR BLUE AND WOULD BE EXPENSIVE FOR RED, which is the point of asking it.
#   sort quality, on the same instrument: cooperative 0.962 against briefed contract 0.750 - one in four
#            contract shooters doubled up on a target a mate already has.
#
# THE GROUND: `nvhas4`, a bunkered defensive position [T1 target kind] at -116.20 behind the merge.
# Campaign rule 3; not attacked. Its callsign differs from w1-03's `nvhas3` on purpose - O5's rule that a
# controlled variant's cast must be disjoint in EVERY unit it can lose, and this pair is a controlled
# variant.
#
# MEASURED (2026-07-30, campaign step 4 AND standalone - fingerprint b690acd9c60de591, identical):
# exit 3, FOUR AIRCRAFT ALIVE, AND THE COOPERATIVE SORT DID NOT SPLIT THE PAIR'S ROUNDS.
#   the sort     **163 `flight SORT_ASSIGN` lines**. `flt_switch` **120** and **41** on the two Blue jets
#                against **1** and **1** on the two aggressors - the cooperative channel is 80 times
#                busier than the briefed contract and it is not better: BOTH Blue AIM-120 went to
#                `rf4agr1` (arrivals 5.934 m and 6.116 m, 0.1 s apart) and nothing was fired at `rf4agr2`
#                until much later. O4-10 measured the same shape at 52/19 against 2/1; W1 measures it at
#                120/41 against 1/1
#   the cover    **0 `flight COVER_DEFER`** on either side, `flt_defer_s` 0.0 on all four,
#                `flt_both_s` 0.0, `flt_exposed_s` 0.3 s on the Blue pair. So the answer to the second
#                half of the question is that the cover rule COST NOTHING - it never fired, because the
#                AIM-120's obligation is 0.3 s and two members were never bound at once
#   the metric   `flt_dup && flt_free > 0` is **0 of 6,000 ticks on all four aircraft**
#   the triggers rf4blu1 t = 128.5 s at 0.981 x Rtr, rf4blu2 t = 128.3 s at 0.980; rf4agr1 t = 127.1 s at
#                0.979, rf4agr2 t = 126.9 s at 0.977. All four within 1.6 s and within 0.004 of Rtr
#   arrivals     nothing killed. Two AIM-120 at 5.93/6.12 m only DEGRADE `rf4agr1` (failed=4088); the
#                aggressors' four R-27R all EXPIRE at 90 s of flight with closest approaches of
#                **15.28 / 17.86 / 22.48 m** against a 13.8 m fuze, and two R-73 at 145 m and 371 m
# THE ONE DEGREE OF FREEDOM COSTS THE WHOLE OUTCOME. w1-03 is this file minus one aircraft a side and it
# ends 0 with a kill; this one ends 3 with nobody hit. That is doc/duels.md's symmetric stalemate arriving
# at force scale, and doc/doctrine-evolution.md already measured its shape - a 2v2 is MORE saturated than
# a 1v1, not less.
#
# WHAT TO READ: `flt_src` (1 = cooperative, 2 = briefed contract), `flt_assign` / `flt_dup` / `flt_switch`
# per jet, `flt_both_s` (seconds two flight-mates were bound at once), `flt_defer_s` (seconds a trigger
# was held to keep the cover) and `flt_exposed_s`; then the per-jet `eng_*` block and every
# `stores DETONATION missM` beside its own `fuzeM`. The violation metric is `flt_dup && flt_free > 0` and
# its required value is zero (doc/formation.md F4) - here, unlike rung 2, there IS something else to
# shoot at, so the metric binds.
#
# READING RULE: exit 3 = TIMEOUT is the expected shape (`kill team hostile` needs BOTH aggressors down);
# the verdict is the flight telemetry read beside w1-03's single-ship numbers. exit 2 would be a defect.

unit rf4blu1
  team friendly
  flight blu4 1
  module f16
  spawn 37.30000 -115.52000 8000 270.0 450
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 80
  set datalink on
  set fcr_mode crm
  set fcr_range_nm 40
  set rwr on
  set store 1 aim120
  set store 2 aim120
  set store 3 aim120
  set store 4 aim120
  set store 6 aim9
  set store 7 aim9
  set cmds_mode auto
  set cmds_program 1
  set cmds_chaff 60
  set cmds_flare 60
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task intercept
  wp 37.30000 -116.58000 8000 450
  objective kill team hostile
  objective survive

unit rf4blu2
  team friendly
  flight blu4 2
  module f16
  spawn 37.28198 -115.52000 8150 270.0 450    # combat spread, 2.0 km abreast, 150 m stack
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 80
  set datalink on
  set fcr_mode crm
  set fcr_range_nm 40
  set rwr on
  set store 1 aim120
  set store 2 aim120
  set store 3 aim120
  set store 4 aim120
  set store 6 aim9
  set store 7 aim9
  set cmds_mode auto
  set cmds_program 1
  set cmds_chaff 60
  set cmds_flare 60
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task intercept
  wp 37.28198 -116.58000 8150 450
  objective kill team hostile
  objective survive

unit rf4agr1
  team hostile
  flight agr4 1
  module mig29
  spawn 37.30000 -116.58000 8000 90.0 450
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 70
  set n019_mode rad
  set n019_range_nm 27
  set n019_emission illum
  set kols_mode ir
  set rwr on
  set brief_sort left                         # the contract: the lead takes the left group
  set store 3 r27r
  set store 4 r27r
  set store 5 r73
  set store 6 r73
  set store 1 r73
  set store 2 r73
  set cmds_mode man
  set cmds_program 1
  set cmds_chaff 30
  set cmds_flare 30
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task intercept
  wp 37.30000 -115.52000 8000 450
  objective kill team friendly
  objective survive

unit rf4agr2
  team hostile
  flight agr4 2
  module mig29
  spawn 37.31802 -116.58000 8150 90.0 450
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 70
  set n019_mode rad
  set n019_range_nm 27
  set n019_emission illum
  set kols_mode ir
  set rwr on
  set brief_sort left                         # the SAME contract; the position decides which end
  set store 3 r27r
  set store 4 r27r
  set store 5 r73
  set store 6 r73
  set store 1 r73
  set store 2 r73
  set cmds_mode man
  set cmds_program 1
  set cmds_chaff 30
  set cmds_flare 30
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task intercept
  wp 37.31802 -115.52000 8150 450
  objective kill team friendly
  objective survive

unit nvhas4
  module target_hard                          # bunkered defensive position [T1 target kind]
  team hostile
  spawn 37.30000 -116.20000 ground 90.0 0
